<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Email on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/email/</link><description>Recent content in Email on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 15 Jan 2009 14:32:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/email/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Inbox</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/inbox/</link><pubDate>Thu, 15 Jan 2009 14:32:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/inbox/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/3198511463/" title="photo sharing"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm4.static.flickr.com/3403/3198511463_7f610a7e08_m.jpg" alt="" style="border: solid 2px #000000;" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style=" margin-top: 0px;font-size:0.9em;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/3198511463/"&gt;Gmail&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Originally uploaded by &lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/people/doodle_m/"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;p&gt;Contents of my Inbox, not that exciting really&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Melt Mail is Another Quick, Disposable Email Service</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/melt-mail-is-another-quick-disposable/</link><pubDate>Wed, 26 Nov 2008 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/melt-mail-is-another-quick-disposable/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 23 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 25 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bloglines.com/"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m melting, melting&amp;hellip;&amp;hellip;&amp;hellip; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;table id="table9477167" bg cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="color:#bde0ed;"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://pipes.yahoo.com/pipes/pipe.info?_id=8IsQFi282xG5FaTJJjBjOg"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Life GH Com&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Pipes Output &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items9477167" style="display: block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: Life GH Com" href="http://feeds.gawker.com/%7Er/lifehacker/full/%7E3/sDwz-jpGTd0/melt-mail-is-another-quick-disposable-email-service"&gt;Melt Mail is Another Quick, Disposable Email Service [Email]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://cache.gawker.com/assets/images/lifehacker/2008/11/melt-mail.png" height="297" width="305" /&gt;Melt Mail is a free email forwarding service that creates a temporary email address that forwards all incoming mail to your real email address. To use it, just enter the email address you want messages forwarded to, select how long you want it to work, then hit Create. Melt Mail generates a random address that you can use with impunity to register on spam-likely sites, for example, and after 3, 6, 12, or 24 hours, the forwarding will stop. We&amp;rsquo;ve &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://lifehacker.com/software/email-forwarding/get-a-temporary-email-address-with-spambox-199943.php"&gt;covered&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://lifehacker.com/software/disposable-email-address/get-a-15+minute-email-address-from-guerrillamail-305933.php"&gt;boat&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://lifehacker.com/software/disposable-email-address/disposable-email-addresses-with-10-minute-mail-287945.php"&gt;loads&lt;/a&gt; of &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://lifehacker.com/software/email/get-a-temporary-email-address-129052.php"&gt;similar&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://lifehacker.com/software/notag/pookmail-disposable-email-addresses-38794.php"&gt;disposable&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://lifehacker.com/software/spam-filters/mailinator-public-spamfree-email-inbox-030870.php"&gt;email&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://lifehacker.com/software/disposable-email-address/avoid-spam-by-registering-with-2-prong-214977.php"&gt;applications&lt;/a&gt;, so Melt Mail isn&amp;rsquo;t breaking any new ground, but since some services won&amp;rsquo;t allow you to register with popular temporary email addresses, it&amp;rsquo;s worthwhile to have another option in your arsenal. Besides, the dead-simple interface is a nice touch. &lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Liberate Yourself from Old Email Addresses [How To]</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/liberate-yourself-from-old-email/</link><pubDate>Mon, 17 Nov 2008 12:23:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/liberate-yourself-from-old-email/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 16 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 19 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bloglines.com/"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;I really need to do this. &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;table id="table9477167" bg cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="color:#bde0ed;"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://pipes.yahoo.com/pipes/pipe.info?_id=8IsQFi282xG5FaTJJjBjOg"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Life GH Com&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Pipes Output &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items9477167" style="display: block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: Life GH Com" href="http://feeds.gawker.com/%7Er/lifehacker/full/%7E3/eHfk89FY-eg/liberate-yourself-from-old-email-addresses"&gt;Liberate Yourself from Old Email Addresses [How To]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://cache.gawker.com/assets/images/lifehacker/2008/11/2008-11-15_194443.jpg" align="left" vspace="2" width="203" height="203" hspace="4" /&gt;If you&amp;rsquo;ve been on the internet for any substantial amount of time you&amp;rsquo;ve likely accumulated your fair share of email addresses. Old school addresses, an assortment of free web-based addresses from Hotmail and Yahoo, and so on all contribute to you having too many addresses and little desire to keep checking the old ones. What can you do to cut down on your email excess? Wired Magazine has a how-to guide to help you consolidate your past email addresses without simply abandoning them into the digital void.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Disposable Email Address Yopmail</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/disposable-email-address-yopmail/</link><pubDate>Fri, 26 Sep 2008 16:09:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/disposable-email-address-yopmail/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 19 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 29 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bloglines.com/"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Could be useful for signing up to dodgy sites :) &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;table id="table9477167" bg cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="color:#bde0ed;"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://pipes.yahoo.com/pipes/pipe.info?_id=8IsQFi282xG5FaTJJjBjOg"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Life GH Com&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Pipes Output &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items9477167" style="display: block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: Life GH Com" href="http://www.ghacks.net/2008/09/25/disposable-email-address-yopmail/"&gt;Disposable Email Address Yopmail&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Disposable email addresses provide the user with an easy to access temporary email address that they can use to register to services on the Internet without having to think about protecting their main email address from spam. While most Internet services are legit and do not sell the email addresses of their users some do sell them. Once an email address is on a spam list it is close to impossible to prevent spam from arriving in the mail inbox.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>